infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Predicate vs assertion: two ways TypeScript narrows
  desc Branch-narrowing handles both cases; scope-narrowing fails loudly on a bug
  compares
    - label Type predicate · x is T
      children
        - label Returns boolean
          desc A value you branch on
        - label Narrows inside the truthy branch only
          desc Outside the if, x is wide again
        - label Branch-narrowing
          desc Use when you handle both cases
    - label Assertion · asserts x is T
      children
        - label Returns void
          desc Throws on the false case
        - label Narrows the rest of the scope after the call
          desc No enclosing branch needed
        - label Scope-narrowing
          desc Use when the false case is a bug
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
